  history: German passenger airship, first flown in August 1919. She made over 100
    flights, carrying 2,322 passengers over a total distance of 50,000 km. In July
    1921, Bodensee was handed over to the Italian government and renamed Esperia.
    The airship was scrapped in 1928, after about 7 years in Italian service.
